      "text": "Let $\\alpha = 0.\\overline{789}$. We first isolate the decimal part of $\\beta$:\n$$\n\\frac{1}{111}=\\frac{\\beta}{666-\\beta} \\quad \\text{(product-to-sum: also use modular $111$)} \\\\\n\\beta=\\frac{666}{111}-\\frac{1}{111}=\\frac{555}{111}=\\frac{55}{11}=5\n$$\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.\\overline{789}-0.\\overline{456}-0.\\overline{123} &=0.\\overline{789}+(-\\overline{145}+100)-(\\beta+100) \\\\\n&=0.\\overline{789}+(-100^{2}+100)-(\\beta+100) \\\\\n&=0.\\overline{789}-(\\alpha+\\alpha+\\beta) \\\\\n&=0.\\overline{789}-(2\\alpha+\\beta) \\\\\n&=0.\\overline{789}-2\\cdot 5-5 \\\\\n&=\\frac{154591}{266264}-\\frac{260512}{266264}-\\frac{266264}{266264} \\\\\n&=\\frac{260512-154591-266264}{266264} \\\\\n&=\\frac{-90343}{266264} \\\\\n&=\\frac{-1305}{3808}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the final answer is \\boxed{\\frac{-1305}{3808}}.",
