      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the value of \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\), we first need to convert each repeating decimal into a fraction.\n\nLet's start with \\(0.\\overline{789}\\). Let \\(x = 0.\\overline{789}\\). Then, \\(1000x = 789.\\overline{789}\\). Subtracting these two equations, we get:\n\\[1000x - x = 789.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{789}\\]\n\\[999x = 789\\]\n\\[x = \\frac{789}{999}\\]\nWe simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 789 and 999, which is 3. So,\n\\[x = \\frac{789 \\div 3}{999 \\div 3} = \\frac{263}{333}\\]\n\nNext, let's convert \\(0.\\overline{456}\\). Let \\(y = 0.\\overline{456}\\). Then, \\(1000y = 456.\\overline{456}\\). Subtracting these two equations, we get:\n\\[1000y - y = 456.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{456}\\]\n\\[999y = 456\\]\n\\[y = \\frac{456}{999}\\]\nWe simplify this fraction by finding the GCD of 456 and 999, which is 3. So,\n\\[y = \\frac{456 \\div 3}{999 \\div 3} = \\frac{152}{333}\\]\n\nFinally, let's convert \\(0.\\overline{123}\\). Let \\(z = 0.\\overline{123}\\). Then, \\(1000z = 123.\\overline{123}\\). Subtracting these two equations, we get:\n\\[1000z - z = 123.\\overline{123} - 0.\\overline{123}\\]\n\\[999z = 123\\]\n\\[z = \\frac{123}{999}\\]\nWe simplify this fraction by finding the GCD of 123 and 999, which is 3. So,\n\\[z = \\frac{123 \\div 3}{999 \\div 3} = \\frac{41}{333}\\]\n\nNow we can calculate \\(0. \\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{263}{333} - \\frac{152}{333} - \\frac{41}{333} = \\frac{263 - 152 - 41}{333} = \\frac{70}{333}\n\\]\nThus, the value is \\(\\frac{70}{333}\\), which is already in its lowest terms.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom math import gcd\r\n\r\n# Fraction parts\r\nnumerator_1 = 263\r\ndenominator_1 = 333\r\n\r\nnumerator_2 = 152\r\ndenominator_2 = 333\r\n\r\nnumerator_3 = 41\r\ndenominator_3 = 333\r\n\r\n# Calculate the gcd for each fraction to simplify\r\ncommon_gcd_1 = gcd(numerator_1, denominator_1)\r\nnumerator_1_simplified = numerator_1 // common_gcd_1\r\ndenominator_1_simplified = denominator_1 // common_gcd_1\r\n\r\ncommon_gcd_2 = gcd(numerator_2, denominator_2)\r\nnumerator_2_simplified = numerator_2 // common_gcd_2\r\ndenominator_2_simplified = denominator_2 // common_gcd_2\r\n\r\ncommon_gcd_3 = gcd(numerator_3, denominator_3)\r\nnumerator_3_simplified = numerator_3 // common_gcd_3\r\ndenominator_3_simplified = denominator_3 // common_gcd_3\r\n\r\n# Final simplified fraction\r\nnumerator_final = numerator_1_simplified - numerator_2_simplified - numerator_3_simplified\r\ndenominator_final = denominator_1_simplified\r\n\r\nsimplified_fraction = (numerator_final, denominator_final)\r\nprint(simplified_fraction)\n```\n```output\n(70, 333)\n```\nThe Python code confirms that the fraction \\(\\frac{70}{333}\\) is in its lowest terms. Therefore, the value of \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{70}{333}}\\).",
